# Four synth keys. The fifth turns the oldest off, on the same bar.
# Drums are not in the count. Full voices: a key that stays on is not thinned.
# Seed 42's intro is pad and hat. Pad is the oldest synth key.
seed 42
reboot
wait 80
expect iammask 65
expect iamlay 0
expect iamdon 16
# Kick and rim, then bass, acid, the fourth, Glass, Dark and Dub, inside this bar.
# Seven synth keys. Pad, bass and acid are the oldest, so they turn off.
# Air, Glass, Dark and Dub stay.
key b0 down
wait 40
key b0 up
key b6 down
wait 40
key b6 up
key w1 down
wait 40
key w1 up
key w2 down
wait 40
key w2 up
key w3 down
wait 40
key w3 up
key w4 down
wait 40
key w4 up
key w5 down
wait 40
key w5 up
key w6 down
wait 40
key w6 up
wait 1500
expect iammask 88
expect iamlay 7
expect iamdon 80
expect iamsec 0
# Stabs comes on. Air is now the oldest, so Air turns off. Stabs stays.
key w7 down
wait 40
key w7 up
wait 1500
expect iammask 80
expect iamlay 15
expect iamdon 80
# Dub turns off and bass comes on, in one bar. Four keys, so nothing is stolen.
key w6 down
wait 40
key w6 up
key w1 down
wait 40
key w1 up
wait 1500
expect iammask 82
expect iamlay 11
expect iamdon 80
# A drum turning off does not free a synth key.
key b0 down
wait 40
key b0 up
wait 1500
expect iammask 66
expect iamlay 11
expect iamdon 80
# Soft comes on. Glass is the oldest still sounding, so Glass turns off. Soft stays.
key w15 down
wait 40
key w15 up
wait 1500
expect iammask 66
expect iamlay 2058
expect iamdon 80
# The kick coming back does not steal a synth key, and does not turn one on.
key b0 down
wait 40
key b0 up
wait 1500
expect iammask 82
expect iamlay 2058
expect iamdon 80
expect iamsec 1
peakreset
wait 1500
expect peak_db_max -0.5
